        "text": "*[Bug 19132] parseNamespaceFile is inconsistent when parsing the importFrom directive*\n<https:\/\/bugs.r-project.org\/show_bug.cgi?id=19132>\n\n--- Comment #9 from Suharto Anggono (<mailto:suharto_anggono@yahoo.com|suharto_anggono@yahoo.com>) ---\nFollowing `coerceVector` in coerce.c where `TYPEOF(x)` is `LANGSXP` and `type`\nis `STRSXP`, but treating symbol (name) specially everywhere, not just the\nfirst element:\n\n```\nvapply(cc,\n       function(e) {\n           if(is.name(e))\n                as.character(e)\n           else if(is.character(e))\n                e\n           else\n                deparse1(e)\n       },\n       \"\")\n```\n\nThe cases of `is.name(e)` and `is.character(e)` can be merged:\n\n```\nvapply(cc,\n       function(e) {\n           if(is.name(e) || is.character(e))\n                as.character(e)\n           else\n                deparse1(e)\n       },\n       \"\")\n```\n\n(In reply to Kurt Hornik from comment #7)\nAbove, should `is.language(e)` be `is.call(e)`?",
